set $S={Z}^{-}\\times {Z}^{-}$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325724 1113 #uuid "532e58fd-76c5-5142-8167-f5bc2c3677bc" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325724 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={Z}^{-}\\times {Z}^{-}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a negative integer and whose $y$-coordinate is a negative integer.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,y\\in {Z}^{-}}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is negative integer.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}={(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}^{-}}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044579/assets/37ad5627c3fb7cc89e751bb697e01ac7fecaf2712e230b6e3812ad9137d5cd46.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{-2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative integer.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-2}={(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}^{-}}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044579/assets/97ebcac85477b8e88564ab67d59c926d5faa72138c8a31d80d3b89895f33668c.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…{S}_{-5},{S}_{-4},{S}_{-3}$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…{S}_{-5}\\cup {S}_{-4}\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1} \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in {Z}^{-}}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${Z}^{-}\\times {Z}^{-}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044579/assets/a756e53554cb9184d96a52b83038fbd6b00b21d0a12cc658aebb5010e917fd03.png)" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325726 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325727 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325728 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325729 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325730 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1041 "selection" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325730 13194139534999 true] [17592186325725 1110 #uuid "49212bd4-a60b-5884-95a7-97caedcf98d9" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325726 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044579/assets/3ea69cc945f29707432415ed194c8abdec6b60056c8c64c845f27b3139cbd3d8.png" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534999 true] [17592186325726 1111 #uuid "ed9ee614-2ae0-58f1-9711-5f7bc6898e24" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325727 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044579/assets/e3550a78d58d91efb3eb012cfad691ee22b7bd216de7910850a289db3ab9e2b2.png" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534999 true] [17592186325727 1111 #uuid "4945781f-823f-51d3-aeba-1a167b61b3c8" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325728 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044579/assets/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534999 true] [17592186325728 1111 #uuid "13d3fbbd-c256-54b5-b6f9-f1d8105450d4" 13194139534999 true] [17592186325729 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044579/assets/35b2f7b26a964f8892ba85bcdeb4fae5312d515044e355cc6a1f989efc8a825c.png" 1319413